player.js: js/vendor/grok-player.js, with one optional buildBody callback added
to buildModel. The original fallback is unchanged when no callback is supplied.
grok-recipes.json: js/vendor/grok-recipes.json, unmodified.

The upstream README labels the repository MIT, but includes no standalone
LICENSE. Its Source section states that the port is for study/research, that
recipes are extracted from the Grok Bot application, and that the underlying
design/data remain their original owners' property. Grok and x.ai trademarks
belong to their owners. The README's MIT label is NOT evidence of permission
to redistribute the extracted animation data in a product.

This experimental integration must not be released until distribution rights
for the source and extracted data are confirmed, or that data is replaced with
independently authored data. No original application bundle is included here.

Non-sphere geometry in the owning geometry.ts is an independent Yuri implementation
of the documented solid/extrusion/loft/seat pipeline. It is not an extracted
renderer and is not asserted to be frame-equivalent to the original app.
